2026-09-27T07:42:30.5436048Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5436596Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5436922Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5437741Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5438652Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5438748Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5438951Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5439255Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5439540Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5439648Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5439863Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5439993Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5440157Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5456823Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5466736Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5466887Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5467228Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5467412Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5467567Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5468014Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5468409Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5469180Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5469805Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5469913Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5470390Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5471001Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5471316Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5471658Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5472120Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5472222Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5472428Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5472540Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5474076Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5475656Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5475973Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5476690Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5477561Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5478199Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5478824Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5547876Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5549043Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5549367Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5549678Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5549840Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5550929Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5552116Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5552780Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5553651Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:30.5553890Z 
